<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to sell Aug 5-10 lifting diesel.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to sell Aug 5-10 lifting diesel.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to sell 225,000-250,000 barrels of diesel for August 5-20 lifting, free-on-board (fob) Kaohsiung, a CPC source said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender for 0.3 percent sulphur diesel closes on July 14 and bids will be valid for two days.</p>
<p>In its last tender, Taiwan sold one cargo for July 23-27 lifting at about 50 cents discount to spot Singapore quotes on an fob basis, traders said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3093)</p>
</text>
